From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:25:13 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: xpon: omci: keep the OLT-G a Set works on when it selects the Nokia profile

omci_agent_set_locked() holds the stored OLT-G object while
omci_agent_profile_refresh_locked() works out the OLT profile from it.
When that selects the Nokia profile on an HGU, the profile seed stores a
default OLT-G ("ALCL", "ISAM") under the same key: omci_mib_store_locked()
replaces the stored object and frees the old one, the one the Set still
holds. The Set then read it in omci_agent_hw_update() and, if a later
step failed, copied the saved state back over it: a read, or a write of
the whole object, in freed kmalloc-2k memory.

One baseline Set from the OLT does it: OLT-G instance 0, OLT vendor ID
"ALCL" or "NOKI" (or an equipment ID naming Nokia or Alcatel), with the
OLT profile on auto and another profile in effect. It became reachable
with 930-416, which creates OLT-G in every profile: before that the Set
was refused with an unknown instance. It also threw away what the OLT
had just written: the stored OLT-G was the seed, with no parsed
identity, so the next refresh from the MIB went back to the generic
profile.

airoha/kernel has the same fix since 8bc68c4c1 ("net: xpon: omci: seed
OLT-G so the OLT can name itself", 2-nov-2026), which added the OLT-G of
every profile there: skip the Nokia seed of OLT-G once the OLT has named
itself. Take that part as it is. In addition, make the Set check that
the refresh left its object in place before using it again, so that a
seed added later cannot bring this back.

Found by reading the source in a security review of the OMCI agent; not
run against a Nokia OLT.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
@@ -1293,7 +1293,13 @@ omci_agent_seed_nokia_locked(struct omci
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 
-		/* Class 131 (OLT-G): pre-seed the Nokia/ALCL OLT identity. */
+		/*
+		 * Class 131 (OLT-G): pre-seed the Nokia/ALCL OLT identity. An
+		 * OLT that named itself is why we are here: its Set is still
+		 * using the object, and its identity is the real one.
+		 */
+		if (omci_agent_olt_g_locked(agent))
+			return 0;
 		memset(data, 0, sizeof(data));
 		memcpy(data, "ALCL", 4);
 		memcpy(data + 4, "ISAM                ", 20);
@@ -4127,6 +4133,17 @@ static u8 omci_agent_set_locked(struct o
 	if (class_id == OMCI_CLASS_OLT_G) {
 		ret = omci_agent_profile_refresh_locked(odev, &object->olt_g,
 							profile_changed);
+		/*
+		 * A profile change rebuilds part of the MIB and has to leave
+		 * this object in place. Should it ever not, the object is
+		 * gone: neither read it nor roll it back.
+		 */
+		if (WARN_ON_ONCE(xa_load(&agent->mib,
+					 omci_mib_key(class_id, entity_id)) !=
+				 object)) {
+			ret = OMCI_RESULT_PROCESSING_ERROR;
+			goto out_free_previous;
+		}
 		if (ret)
 			goto rollback_processing;
 	}
